model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway.appCalls {
    metadata {
      constraint "Selected-account reads use the verified original viewer and grant, never a saved app-call authorizer, and recheck native selections, generations and every dependency connection before returning. Their linked-app lookup stays independent of account handlers and lifecycle code so shared authentication does not retain provider-app code in SSO. Worker measurements use ignored local output; preflight rejects carried measurement scripts and staged or newly committed literals matching secret-named environment values without logging those values. Existing connections retain exact targets for many-target declarations; omitted cardinality keeps one-target replacement. SDK storage 4.0.30 changes only the target-binding index while released 4.0.27 through 4.0.29 schemas remain frozen. Native selection setup backfills only one proven installed provider-app holder; ambiguity retains existing presentation, revoked or invalid saved sources withhold copied presentation, and no source state changes pool membership or routing. Protocol 41 adds optional selected-account read controls while released dependency wire schemas remain unchanged."
    }
  }
}
